# ZIMO — example environment file
# ===================================================================
# EVERYTHING HERE IS OPTIONAL in the default (bridge) mode. ZIMO runs
# perfectly with an empty file — the bridge authenticates off your Claude Code
# login, and voice input and output both fall back to the browser's own speech.
# Copy this to .env.local, and add only what you actually want to change.
#
# The one line worth adding is ELEVENLABS_API_KEY, down in the BRIDGE section:
# it gives you a much better voice and Scribe transcription. The free tier is
# plenty for a demo. Never commit a real key.
#
# Two audiences read these variables:
#   - the BRIDGE (the Node server, bridge/server.mjs) reads the ZIMO_* and
#     ELEVENLABS_API_KEY variables from its shell environment.
#   - the FRONTEND (the Vite app) reads the VITE_* variables from .env.local.
# Only VITE_-prefixed values ever reach the browser.


# ===================================================================
# BRIDGE (the server) — read from the shell that runs `npm run bridge`
# ===================================================================
# These are shown with their defaults. Leave them unset to accept the default.

# Port the bridge listens on (WebSocket + a few HTTP endpoints). Default 8787.
# If you change it, change VITE_BRIDGE_URL to match.
# ZIMO_BRIDGE_PORT=8787

# The model the bridge asks Claude Code to run. Default claude-opus-5.
# ZIMO_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# Reasoning effort. Default medium.
# ZIMO_EFFORT=medium

# Allow effectful tools (send, tap, delete, install, pay). Off by default, so
# ZIMO can look at anything and change nothing. `npm run bridge:writes` sets
# this to 1 for you — read the decideTool gate in bridge/server.mjs first.
# ZIMO_ALLOW_WRITES=0

# Extra browser origins allowed to open the agent WebSocket, comma separated.
# Local dev origins are already allowed; add others only if you serve the app
# from a different address. Default: none.
# ZIMO_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=

# Allow clients that send no Origin header at all (curl, scripts, native apps).
# Off by default, because that is also what local malware looks like. Default 0.
# ZIMO_ALLOW_NO_ORIGIN=0

# Passphrase the bridge requires on every socket connection and HTTP request
# (except /health). Must match VITE_ZIMO_PASSWORD below or nothing connects.
# Default '4564' — a 4-digit PIN is fine for "don't let another tab drive this
# by accident" but is not real security against anyone who can reach the port
# and try a few thousand guesses. Set your own before trusting this on a LAN.
# ZIMO_PASSWORD=4564

# Extra directories the bridge's /file endpoint may serve from, comma separated.
# Your home directory and the system temp directory are always included; this is
# for anything outside them, such as an external drive of footage. Default: none.
# ZIMO_FILE_ROOTS=

# ElevenLabs voice id for the bridge's own speech endpoint. Default: George.
# ZIMO_VOICE_ID=JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb

# ElevenLabs API key. Optional. With it, ZIMO speaks in the ElevenLabs voice
# and transcribes with ElevenLabs Scribe; without it, everything still works on
# the browser's own speech. If you already have an elevenlabs MCP server in
# ~/.claude.json, the bridge reads the key from there and you can leave this
# blank. Default: none.
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# Run `npm run list-voices` after setting this to see every voice on your
# account and its id, instead of guessing — then set ZIMO_VOICE_ID above.
# VITE_ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BRAIN — which model actually thinks. Default claude, and the only one with
# the full tool loop (HUD, MCP servers, browser control). See bridge/brain.mjs.
# Swap anytime by saying or typing "switch brain to hermes" — no restart.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# claude | hermes | ollama | hf. Default claude.
# ZIMO_BRAIN=claude

# Hermes 4 (Nous Research), served through OpenRouter. Needed only for
# ZIMO_BRAIN=hermes. Get one at openrouter.ai.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# HERMES_MODEL=nousresearch/hermes-4-405b

# A local Ollama model — the fully offline, fully swappable option. Needed
# only for ZIMO_BRAIN=ollama. Install from ollama.com, then `ollama pull` any
# model and put its name below.
# OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434
# OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.1

# Hugging Face Inference Providers — a free tier across a wide catalogue of
# open models (Llama, Qwen, Mistral, DeepSeek and more) behind one endpoint.
# Needed only for ZIMO_BRAIN=hf. Get a free token at
# huggingface.co/settings/tokens (Read access is enough).
# HF_TOKEN=
# HF_MODEL=meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct

# Also used, regardless of ZIMO_BRAIN, as a fallback debugger: when a Claude
# turn fails, the bridge asks whichever of hf/hermes/ollama has credentials
# configured for a second opinion on what went wrong (see diagnoseError in
# bridge/brain.mjs). Set HF_TOKEN (or one of the others) even if you never
# plan to switch brains, just to get that safety net.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OBSIDIAN — second brain. Needs the "Local REST API" community plugin
# installed and enabled inside Obsidian itself first. See bridge/obsidian.mjs
# for the three-step setup. Optional; without it the obsidian_* tools just
# explain what to do instead of failing silently.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The API key the Local REST API plugin generates in its own settings tab.
# OBSIDIAN_API_KEY=

# host:port the plugin listens on. Default 127.0.0.1:27124 (https, self-signed).
# OBSIDIAN_HOST=127.0.0.1:27124

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SELF-HEAL — fully autonomous crash recovery. Off unless you run it via
# `npm run start:heal` (which sets ZIMO_SELF_HEAL=1 for you). Read
# bridge/selfheal.mjs and scripts/self-heal-supervisor.mjs before turning this
# on anywhere but your own machine: on a crash, it lets Claude edit files
# under bridge/ and src/ with no human approval step, then restarts the
# process. Every patch is snapshotted first and syntax/type-checked before
# it's trusted — a bad patch is rolled back automatically — but "no approval
# step" is still the honest description of what this does.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# `npm run start:heal` instead of `npm run bridge`. Everything below is
# optional; the defaults are what that command uses.

# Model used for the heal attempt itself. Default claude-opus-5.
# ZIMO_HEAL_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# Cap on self-heal attempts within the window below, before the supervisor
# gives up and leaves the bridge down rather than loop forever. Default 5.
# ZIMO_SELF_HEAL_MAX_ATTEMPTS=5
# ZIMO_SELF_HEAL_WINDOW_MS=3600000

# Separate, tighter cap on plain restarts (a crash with no usable report to
# heal from, or self-heal simply off). Default 10 restarts / 5 minutes.
# ZIMO_MAX_PLAIN_RESTARTS=10

# Where ZIMO's memory, profile and settings live on this machine. Default
# ~/.zimo. Change it if you want his home somewhere other than your user
# folder — an external drive, a synced folder, whatever "this laptop" means
# to you.
# ZIMO_HOME=


# ===================================================================
# FRONTEND (Vite) — put these in .env.local
# ===================================================================

# Which brain the browser talks to. Default bridge.
#   bridge — talk to the local bridge (recommended). No API key, and every MCP
#            server in your Claude Code config is available.
#   direct — the browser calls the Claude API itself. Needs VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.
# VITE_BACKEND=bridge

# Where the bridge listens. Keep the port in step with ZIMO_BRIDGE_PORT above.
# Default ws://localhost:8787.
# VITE_BRIDGE_URL=ws://localhost:8787

# Must match ZIMO_PASSWORD above exactly, or every connection to the bridge —
# socket and HTTP alike — gets refused. Default '4564'.
# VITE_ZIMO_PASSWORD=4564

# Browser text-to-speech engine, used when no ElevenLabs voice is active.
# Default system.
#   system — the browser's built-in speechSynthesis. Instant, on-device.
#   kokoro — a neural voice running in the browser. Better sound, slower to start.
# VITE_TTS_ENGINE=system

# Which Kokoro voice, when VITE_TTS_ENGINE=kokoro. Default bm_george.
# VITE_KOKORO_VOICE=bm_george

# Prefer the ElevenLabs voice from the browser when a key is available.
# Default false.
# VITE_USE_ELEVENLABS=false

# Anthropic API key — DIRECT MODE ONLY. Required if and only if
# VITE_BACKEND=direct, and it ships to the browser, so use it only for a local
# demo. The default bridge mode never reads it. Default: none.
# VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Your name, shown on the standby screen ("Hello, ‹name›"). Purely cosmetic —
# stays in the browser, never sent anywhere. Default: none (shows "Hello").
# VITE_USER_NAME=
